{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/98267-manslaughter-clarity-4-but-killing-human-clarity-2","id":98267,"title":"Manslaughter clarity 4 but killing human clarity 2?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-25T04:46:23-07:00","id":98267,"title":"Manslaughter clarity 4 but killing human clarity 2?","content":"How in Earth does that work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2585-alejandro","name":"Alejandro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T04:58:06-07:00","id":98272,"title":"","content":"Manslaughter is usually unintentional (a car accident, for instance). Murder is not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-25-2014, 08:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T05:17:28-07:00","id":98283,"title":"","content":"But it doesnt say MURDER human is sin to cliarity 2. It says KILL human is sin to clarity 2 Besides, there is both voluntary (intentional) manslaugther and involuntary (unintentional) manslaugther.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2585-alejandro","name":"Alejandro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T06:50:23-07:00","id":98310,"title":"","content":"You know the difference, so is your problem with the wording? It specifically refers to Impassioned or impulsive serious crimes when it mentions manslaughter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T06:52:35-07:00","id":98313,"title":"","content":"@ Alejandro<br /> So? Unless it's a misprint, the text is pretty evidently trying to make exactly the distinction Nofather pointed out. It's an RPG book not a legal text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":178,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","user":"Michael","date":". 03-25-2014, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T12:03:21-07:00","id":98541,"title":"","content":"I dont understand. If a changeling commits manslaugther, he needs to be killing someone, either human or changeling, but someone. &quot;Kill&quot; is a way less strict term than manslaugther so it is very weird it is at clarity 2. I truly dont know how you could see that text as &quot;clear&quot; and I am no lawyer, I simply did a quick and easy wiki search to know what manslaugther was and there was the difference I said. Even if it was what nofather said, you cannot accidentally kill a human without actually killing the human so the problem persists. So I dont understand, you cannot commit manslaugther without killing a human, how can manslaugther be less grave?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2585-alejandro","name":"Alejandro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T12:39:43-07:00","id":98570,"title":"","content":"The implication seems to be impassioned, accidental or self-defense killing vs, straight going in and killing the bastard. The clarity 4 sin seems pretty clear on it, 2 less so, but 2 makes sense when examined in conjunction with 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T13:34:03-07:00","id":98615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I truly dont know how you could see that text as &quot;clear&quot; </div> </div> </div>I didn't say it was clear. I said it was evident. I'm specifically not saying it's clear, because it's not. My point was the same as Baron Samedi; that from the context you can work out what was intended by the author.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and I am no lawyer, I simply did a quick and easy wiki search to know what manslaugther was and there was the difference I said. </div> </div> </div>That's not my point. I was saying that RPG rules are not legal documents in the sense that they aren't generally written to be followed blindly and therefore they aren't written with the same level of care and you just have to live with that. They used KILL to mean MURDER, deal with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T00:00:21-07:00","id":99800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/98267-manslaughter-clarity-4-but-killing-human-clarity-2?p=98615#post98615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I didn't say it was clear. I said it was evident. I'm specifically not saying it's clear, because it's not. My point was the same as Baron Samedi; that from the context you can work out what was intended by the author. That's not my point. I was saying that RPG rules are not legal documents in the sense that they aren't generally written to be followed blindly and therefore they aren't written with the same level of care and you just have to live with that. They used KILL to mean MURDER, deal with it.</div> </div> </div> </div> You could have just aaid &quot;i think it was a missprint they meant to say murder not kill&quot; in e first place. Whatever it is that hs happened to you that made you this offensive to me, it just honestly didnt came from me o.0","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2585-alejandro","name":"Alejandro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T00:06:18-07:00","id":99804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/98267-manslaughter-clarity-4-but-killing-human-clarity-2?p=98570#post98570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The implication seems to be impassioned, accidental or self-defense killing vs, straight going in and killing the bastard. The clarity 4 sin seems pretty clear on it, 2 less so, but 2 makes sense when examined in conjunction with 4.</div> </div> </div> </div> I d say its straightforward a missprint or bad editing. I guess what you say makes sense. I am still a bit naive expecting them not to make this big of a mistake in the core book nd text I guess <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So they actually wanted to say &quot;murder&quot; (probably even premeditated murder? ) human... I think I am going to rule this kind of things with fetches and changelings (and maybe other supernaturals) to be one less grave than they would if humans. They make. Distinction in gravity about humans and fetches/changelings (wch very interestingly are in the same pocket there) and I think I ll house rule mantain it on others as it make sense to me. I guess what made it more confusing to me was that the way written is the same they wrote kill changeling or fetch. I wonder if I should read that as &quot;murder&quot; changeling or fetch then, but then that sounds extremely more cheap on changeling and fetch life than I would expect for what comes to clarity o.o What would be your take on that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2585-alejandro","name":"Alejandro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T13:03:24-07:00","id":100276,"title":"","content":"One thing is the way people use Manslaughter colloquially often has less gravitas then killing. It means essentially that you killed them, but has a layer of separation in a lot of people's minds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T14:14:39-07:00","id":100332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You could have just aaid &quot;i think it was a missprint they meant to say murder not kill&quot; in e first place. Whatever it is that hs happened to you that made you this offensive to me, it just honestly didnt came from me o.0 </div> </div> </div>Ok ok, sorry. It's just that it's difficult to seperate people who have genuine issues with the language from people who are being legalistic rules lawyers for the sake of argument.<br /> <br /> Adding to what Baron Samedi said, it's not so much that the text is wrong so much as it's written in an ambiguous manner and it assumes that groups will rely heavily on their own common sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T15:47:51-07:00","id":100412,"title":"","content":"In my games, I've actually taken it in a different direction. Degrees of murder/manslaughter largely got tossed out the window. For Changelings, killing any human, in any way, is a grave sin that resembles the callous disregard for human life that the Others demonstrate far too much to preserve high Clarity. Hence Clarity 2. Changelings and Fetches are Fae creatures, and killing them, disturbingly, is almost like a game or story in and of itself. It doesn't feel real, and so killing them is just Clarity 5 (I think, would need to double-check the book here).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T02:51:29-07:00","id":100658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/98267-manslaughter-clarity-4-but-killing-human-clarity-2?p=100276#post100276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing is the way people use Manslaughter colloquially often has less gravitas then killing. It means essentially that you killed them, but has a layer of separation in a lot of people's minds.</div> </div> </div> </div> I must have missed this as English is not my first language then, so while a lot or most coloquialisms may be nkown by me (say, movie coloquialisms xD) man salugther doesnt precisely sound less grave to me. To me kill is a watered phrase, like &quot;i just killed a mosquitoe&quot; while anything with the word slaugther in it sounds like a mess xD. Now I understand then it wa a coloquialism <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2585-alejandro","name":"Alejandro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T02:52:50-07:00","id":100660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/98267-manslaughter-clarity-4-but-killing-human-clarity-2?p=100332#post100332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ok ok, sorry. It's just that it's difficult to seperate people who have genuine issues with the language from people who are being legalistic rules lawyers for the sake of argument. Adding to what Baron Samedi said, it's not so much that the text is wrong so much as it's written in an ambiguous manner and it assumes that groups will rely heavily on their own common sense.</div> </div> </div> </div> Groups will definetely do, but &quot;common sense &quot; varies heavily among different people. There are a lot of senses common to a lot of people and contradictory to other &quot;common senses&quot; if you know what I mean. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2585-alejandro","name":"Alejandro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T02:57:20-07:00","id":100663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/98267-manslaughter-clarity-4-but-killing-human-clarity-2?p=100412#post100412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my games, I've actually taken it in a different direction. Degrees of murder/manslaughter largely got tossed out the window. For Changelings, killing any human, in any way, is a grave sin that resembles the callous disregard for human life that the Others demonstrate far too much to preserve high Clarity. Hence Clarity 2. Changelings and Fetches are Fae creatures, and killing them, disturbingly, is almost like a game or story in and of itself. It doesn't feel real, and so killing them is just Clarity 5 (I think, would need to double-check the book here).</div> </div> </div> </div> I was honestly thinking along side this when I read that too. Specially since you are right, it is sin to claritive five to KILL (not manslaugther or anything) a fetch or a changeling. Now, that I think of it, given the interpretation I now understand is given to kill (pretty much murder) this would mean planning a murder on a fetch and killing him is mere sin five still. My characters are planning pretty much to torture them both physically and psychologically (onf em truly diserves it while the other one really is just there to be a &quot;button&quot; to push on the fetch that does diserve it as he is in love with her) and then kill em. Her first so he can watch and suffer a lot. I was thinking it could be clarity one if they were humans but to push it to clarity 2 for them being fetches. How would you guys handle it at your tables?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2585-alejandro","name":"Alejandro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T13:16:52-07:00","id":100844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alejandro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/98267-manslaughter-clarity-4-but-killing-human-clarity-2?p=100658#post100658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I must have missed this as English is not my first language then, so while a lot or most coloquialisms may be nkown by me (say, movie coloquialisms xD) man salugther doesnt precisely sound less grave to me. To me kill is a watered phrase, like &quot;i just killed a mosquitoe&quot; while anything with the word slaugther in it sounds like a mess xD. Now I understand then it wa a coloquialism <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that might be the case. It seems to be used somewhat lightly sometimes. I understand objectively that seems odd.<br /> <br /> ETA: I generally have torturing anyone Clarity (or most other moralities) 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 03-28-2014, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T13:45:03-07:00","id":100856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Groups will definetely do, but &quot;common sense &quot; varies heavily among different people. There are a lot of senses common to a lot of people and contradictory to other &quot;common senses&quot; if you know what I mean. </div> </div> </div>I think that's the point. It's up to the troupe to decide how hard you want the morality rules to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T01:54:10-07:00","id":101146,"title":"","content":"So, in the end then how should I understand clarity 5 sin of &quot;killing&quot; a fetch or changeling? Should I understand it as murder? Murder a fetch or changeling is just clarity 5 ? Should I understand it as manslaugther? I understand there are things left for the group to decide, but I do feel the clarity chart could/sshould have been more clear there. Does it mean that even murder to changeling is just clarity 5? Just like in clarity 2 kill meant murder? And michael, what would you rule at your table as the clarity roll for what I said above?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2585-alejandro","name":"Alejandro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T01:56:48-07:00","id":101150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/98267-manslaughter-clarity-4-but-killing-human-clarity-2?p=100844#post100844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I thought that might be the case. It seems to be used somewhat lightly sometimes. I understand objectively that seems odd. ETA: I generally have torturing anyone Clarity (or most other moralities) 1.</div> </div> </div> </div> Makes sense. I usually go torture anyone anything 2, and if its torture for the sake of torture probably 1. Just n this case thinking maybe I will assume it a 2 for being a fetch. That said I will definetely give him a derangement for the issue if only a temporal one, so he ll be rolling for the clarity rule about derangements too. The derangement just tl the one who is doing this to his fetch, as he is torturing a part of his soul and well, seeing himself in deep pain in front of himself and knowing its his doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2585-alejandro","name":"Alejandro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}